sequenceDiagram
  participant W as words = [eat, tea, tan, ate]
  participant G as groups (key to list of words)
  W->>G: eat: key = a1 e1 t1, new key
  G-->>W: groups[a1 e1 t1] = [eat]
  W->>G: tea: key = a1 e1 t1, key exists
  G-->>W: groups[a1 e1 t1] = [eat, tea]
  W->>G: tan: key = a1 n1 t1, new key
  G-->>W: groups[a1 n1 t1] = [tan]
  W->>G: ate: key = a1 e1 t1, key exists
  G-->>W: groups[a1 e1 t1] = [eat, tea, ate]
  Note over W,G: answer: 2 groups. Each word is read once and its key is built in one pass over its letters.
